# Claude Security -- suggested patch for F1: Stored XSS: buyer-supplied rating comment rendered via innerHTML after bypassSecurityTrustHtml
# Applies to revision d5dab2155552 (the revision these patches were built against).
#
# Verified by a panel of agents: an independent verifier reviewed this
# change against the finding, and a second, fresh reviewer challenged the
# diff for an attack path it opens, or a route it leaves open to the
# finding's exploit. The patch was written only because the panel stated
# all three of these with confidence:
#   - the change is highly targeted to this finding: the diff touches only rating-list.component.ts: the bypass call, the import and injection that existed only to serve it, and the related comment and return type; the other changes in HEAD are left alone
#   - the change introduces no new security vulnerability: the change only re-enables Angular's default [innerHTML] sanitization at rating-list.component.html:19; nothing is loosened, no new sink or input is added, and the component is used only by routing and DI
#   - beyond closing the finding, the change does not alter the code's behaviour or the inputs it accepts: review only: plain-text comments and safe formatting render the same through the same binding; only the injected-markup class the finding names (event handlers, script, javascript: URLs, inline style) is stripped
#
# NOTE: no project test of the patched code was run. The claim that
# behaviour is unchanged rests on review of the change and its callers,
# not on a test run -- weigh it accordingly before applying.
#
# RatingListComponent.commentHtml marked the buyer's raw comment trusted with bypassSecurityTrustHtml before the [innerHTML] binding; the patch returns the plain string so Angular's built-in HTML sanitizer runs, and drops the now-unused DomSanitizer injection.
# Tests run: none possible: npm test -- --watch=false in web/ failed with 'ng: not found' (no web/node_modules in the workspace, and dependencies were not installed)
#
# Apply, from the repository root:  git apply CLAUDE-SECURITY-20261016-151158/patches/F1.patch
#
diff --git a/web/src/app/ratings/rating-list/rating-list.component.ts b/web/src/app/ratings/rating-list/rating-list.component.ts
